Feature: Placement Workbench — Stable Video & Visible Surfaces
  As an editor reviewing ad placements
  I want the placement workbench to be stable and show detected surfaces clearly
  So that I can efficiently review and approve surface placements without UI glitches

  Background:
    Given I am logged in as an Editor
    And I have a campaign with completed video content
    And scene detection has been run on the video

  Scenario: Video player does not reload or flash during review
    Given I am on the Placement Workbench viewing a video
    When background data polling occurs (renders, logs, alarms)
    Then the video player does NOT unmount or reload
    And the video playback position is maintained
    And the SVG surface overlay remains visible

  Scenario: Surfaces are clearly visible as colored polygons on the video
    Given a video has detected surfaces
    When I view the Placement Workbench
    Then all detected surfaces are shown as colored semi-transparent polygons overlaid on the video
    And non-selected surfaces have a subtle pulse animation to draw attention
    And each surface polygon has a visible colored outline with outer glow

  Scenario: Clicking a surface in the list jumps to the correct frame
    Given the Detected Surfaces list shows multiple surfaces
    When I click on a surface card in the list
    Then the video seeks to approximately 1/3 into the scene containing that surface
    And the video pauses to show the frame
    And the clicked surface is highlighted with a glow effect
    And the surface detail panel updates to show that surface's metadata

  Scenario: Surface thumbnails are displayed in the list
    Given a surface has a generated thumbnail (PlacementImageUrl)
    When I view the Detected Surfaces list
    Then each surface card shows a small thumbnail preview image
    And surfaces without thumbnails show a placeholder icon

  Scenario: Surface thumbnail is shown in the detail panel
    Given I have selected a surface with a thumbnail
    When I view the Surface Details panel
    Then a full-width thumbnail image is displayed above the metadata

  Scenario: SVG overlay aligns with letterboxed video
    Given a video with non-16:9 aspect ratio
    When the video is displayed with object-contain (letterboxed)
    Then the SVG surface overlay is letterboxed identically
    And surface polygon coordinates align with the displayed video content

  Scenario: Placement workbench renders even when no videos are completed
    Given there are no videos with "Completed" status
    When I navigate to the Placement Workbench
    Then the workbench layout is still rendered (not hidden)
    And an informational message is shown guiding the user to upload content first

  Scenario: Background polling does not disrupt content state
    Given I am viewing content on the Placement Workbench
    When the 10-second operational data poll executes
    Then contentList, campaignList, and assetList are NOT updated
    And only renderList, logList, and alarmList are refreshed
